    "summary": "This sword has a straight <em>kalis</em> blade with squared shoulders, a long central fuller, and an engraved chevron-and-scroll pattern above the guard. The wing guards at the base of the blade are held in place by two <em>asang-asang</em> (fish gill) clamps. The hilt terminates with a silver cockatoo (<em>kakatua</em>)-shaped pommel. Silver pommels of this type are associated with elite <em>datu</em> owners.",
